# Asymmetry 6 — four player units against two elites and a fisherman.
# A pit trench spans the board; the only two crossings are the outer columns, and an
# Anchor is standing in each. Push 1 does nothing to an Anchor, so the doors need
# a Bull Rush or a Reel — one key each, one per player.
#   .  open        #  wall        O  pit        ^  spikes      H  high ground
#   A  Player A deploy slot       B  Player B deploy slot
#   any other letter = an enemy declared by a 'spawn' line below

id: as-06-immovable
number: 406
name: Immovable
description: Two Anchors plug the only two bridges over the trench and shrug off every Push 1 on the board. Four units, two doors, two different keys.
retired: Both bridge Anchors step off their bridges in round 1. Premise dead; `hz-09` owns the question.

spawn g = Grappler
spawn n = Anchor

roster a: Vanguard, Wardbearer
roster b: Archer, Threadcaster

board:
